# slack trigger tests (mention + activated-thread filter)
#   ✓ plain message with no mention and no active thread → NOT triggered
#   ✓ message with @mention → triggered and thread root activated
#   ✓ app_mention event type → triggered even without text mention
#   ✓ reply in activated thread without re-mention → triggered
#   ✓ bot's own threaded reply (bot_id) → NOT triggered (self-loop safety)
#   ✓ subtype message (e.g. message_changed) → NOT triggered
#   ✓ mention in a reply → activates ev.thread_ts (not ev.ts)
#   ✓ wrong channel → NOT triggered even with mention
#   ✓ matching channel → triggered
#   ✓ no channel filter (null) → any channel triggers
#   ✓ activatedThreads evicts oldest when cap is reached
#   ✓ default cap is ACTIVATED_THREADS_MAX
#   ✓ botUserId null → text mention not detected (app_mention still works)
#   ✓ null/undefined event → NOT triggered
#   ✓ file_share + @mention → triggered and files extracted
#   ✓ file_share in activated thread (no re-mention) → triggered
#   ✓ file_share with no mention and no activated thread → NOT triggered
#   ✓ other subtype (message_changed) even with files → NOT triggered
#   ✓ files without url_private are filtered out
#   ✓ files capped at MAX_FILES_PER_MESSAGE (10)
#   ✓ text-only trigger still returns empty files array
#   ✓ sanitizeSlackFilename: blocks path traversal and special chars
#   ✓ bot token is NOT included in files array sent via IPC (structural check)
#   ✓ dedupKey is identical for app_mention and message events of the SAME message
#   ✓ dedupKey returns "" when channel or ts is missing (uncacheable)
#   ✓ SeenEvents.seen: first occurrence false (new), repeat true (duplicate)
#   ✓ SeenEvents never dedupes empty/falsy keys (and does not store them)
#   ✓ SeenEvents is bounded FIFO — oldest key evicted past the cap
#   ✓ SEEN_EVENTS_MAX default is exported and sane
#   ✓ integration: dual-subscription double-fire collapses to ONE delivery
